# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "September 2026 {#september-2026}"
msgstr "Setyembre 2026 {#september-2026}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "New tools have been built on top of the [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model) framework, which was released earlier this year:\n"
msgstr "May mga bagong tool na binuo sa ibabaw ng framework ng [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model), na inilabas nang mas maaga ngayong taon:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`qiskit-noise-learning`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-noise-learning) is a toolkit for randomization-based quantum noise characterization. You can use it to construct a custom noise-learning experiment, validate it with local simulation, and analyze the raw results.\n"
msgstr "Ang [`qiskit-noise-learning`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-noise-learning) ay isang toolkit para sa randomization-based na quantum noise characterization. Magagamit mo ito para bumuo ng custom na noise-learning experiment, i-validate ito gamit ang local simulation, at suriin ang mga raw na resulta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`qiskit-mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) is a package of quantum error mitigation methods for building mitigation pipelines with the new execution model. It includes implementations of well-known methods, including PEC, PEA, TREX, and gate-folding ZNE, as well as post-selection for filtering out non-Markovian errors.\n"
msgstr "Ang [`qiskit-mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) ay isang package ng mga paraan ng quantum error mitigation para sa pagbuo ng mga mitigation pipeline gamit ang bagong execution model. Kasama rito ang mga implementasyon ng mga kilalang paraan, kabilang ang PEC, PEA, TREX, at gate-folding ZNE, pati na rin ang post-selection para sa pag-filter ng mga non-Markovian na error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "August 2026 {#august-2026}"
msgstr "Agosto 2026 {#august-2026}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Qiskit Fermions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) had its first release this month! This package provides tools for working with fermionic systems, including building fermionic operators and circuits, implementing fermion-to-qubit encodings, and circuit synthesis through the Qiskit transpiler integration. Qiskit Fermions can be used with other complementary tools in the ecosystem, such as `ffsim` (see this [documentation](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) and [blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/ffsim) for more information) and the [SQD addon](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd), to build advanced workflows for fermionic systems. \n"
msgstr "Inilabas na ang unang release ng [Qiskit Fermions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) ngayong buwan! Nagbibigay ang package na ito ng mga tool para sa pagtatrabaho sa mga fermionic system, kabilang ang pagbuo ng mga fermionic operator at circuit, pag-implement ng fermion-to-qubit encoding, at circuit synthesis sa pamamagitan ng integrasyon ng Qiskit transpiler. Maaaring gamitin ang Qiskit Fermions kasama ng iba pang komplementaryong tool sa ecosystem, tulad ng `ffsim` (tingnan ang [dokumentasyon](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) at [blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/ffsim) na ito para sa karagdagang impormasyon) at ang [SQD addon](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd), para bumuo ng mga advanced na workflow para sa mga fermionic system. \n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "See how these tools are applied in practice with the [SqDRIFT algorithm for ground state estimation](/tutorials/sqdrift) tutorial and the following guide: [Building constant-depth circuits to simulate the dynamics of the 1- and 2-D Fermi-Hubbard model](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions/guides/1-d-fermi-hubbard). Check out the [blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qiskit-fermions) and [documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) to get started.\n"
msgstr "Tingnan kung paano ginagamit ang mga tool na ito sa praktika sa tutorial na [SqDRIFT algorithm for ground state estimation](/tutorials/sqdrift) at sa sumusunod na guide: [Building constant-depth circuits to simulate the dynamics of the 1- and 2-D Fermi-Hubbard model](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions/guides/1-d-fermi-hubbard). Tingnan ang [blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qiskit-fermions) at [dokumentasyon](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) para makapagsimula.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "June 2026 {#june-2026}"
msgstr "Hunyo 2026 {#june-2026}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introducing [Qiskit Paulice](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice): a new addon that integrates low-overhead quantum error detection into quantum circuits to boost the fidelity of measured distributions. It provides single-shot access to the quantum state and so can be used in both sampling-based and expectation value-based workflows. Check out the [blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qiskit-paulice) and [documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice) for how to get started today.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakilala ang [Qiskit Paulice](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice): isang bagong addon na nagsasama ng mababang-overhead na quantum error detection sa mga quantum circuit para mapahusay ang fidelity ng mga sinukat na distribution. Nagbibigay ito ng single-shot na access sa quantum state kaya magagamit ito sa parehong sampling-based at expectation value-based na mga workflow. Tingnan ang [blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qiskit-paulice) at [dokumentasyon](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice) para malaman kung paano magsimula ngayon.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Previous updates {#previous-updates}"
msgstr "Mga nakaraang update {#previous-updates}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We recently released two new addons that use classical resources to reduce the quantum resources needed for error mitigation:\n"
msgstr "Kamakailan lang kaming naglabas ng dalawang bagong addon na gumagamit ng mga classical resource para bawasan ang mga quantum resource na kailangan para sa error mitigation:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Propagated noise absorption (PNA)](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-pna/) is a technique for mitigating errors in expectation values by absorbing the inverses of the learned noise channels into observables using Pauli propagation. \n"
msgstr "Ang [Propagated noise absorption (PNA)](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-pna/) ay isang teknik para mabawasan ang mga error sa expectation values sa pamamagitan ng pag-absorb ng mga inverse ng mga natutunang noise channel sa mga observable gamit ang Pauli propagation. \n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [Shaded lightcones (SLC)](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/) addon uses classical simulations to more tightly bound the sensitivity to errors throughout the circuit. This allows for more efficient, targeted applications of Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) with reduced variance.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng [Shaded lightcones (SLC)](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/) addon ang mga classical simulation para mas mahigpit na matantya ang hangganan ng sensitivity sa mga error sa buong circuit. Dahil dito, mas episyente at mas nakatutok ang paggamit ng Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC), at mas mababa ang variance.\n"
